  "claim": "On host nativestack-5975wx-20260925 on 2026-09-25, rtk 0.50.0 was qualified against the installed 0.49.0 on the Claude Code hook path and then switched into production. The rtk-ai/rtk v0.50.0 asset rtk-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz hashed to sha256 bc2b8902b0d9c796c82ef45f16ae2307e17757afeca5ee156235a3dc7bda5f89, equal to its checksums.txt line (sha256sum --check --strict: OK) and to the GitHub API asset digest, and was installed into a new tools/rtk-0.50.0 prefix (binary sha256 23433a2a50bdeb12199cadd4b94b639238d6c38529fcba1c30c9295db5fa9517). Driving `rtk hook claude` with Claude PreToolUse JSON and scratch data directories, the hash-pinned acceptance scripts gave 42 PASS / 0 FAIL / 1 NOTE (v2, sha256 186dd891...) and 88 PASS / 0 FAIL / 4 NOTE (v3.1, sha256 3644a0dc...) for 0.50.0, against 34/8/1 and 79/9/4 for 0.49.0; v3.1 rejected two broken fake candidates (4/100/11 and 17/85/11), and `rtk verify` passed 154/154 on both versions. An independent verifier re-ran these, reproduced the outputs line for line and agreed. The coordinator then repointed bin/rtk to the new prefix (`rtk --version`: rtk 0.50.0) and created ~/.config/rtk/config.toml with `exclude_commands = [\"^git show [^ ]*:\", \"diff\"]`. v3.1 on the production binary gave 87 PASS / 1 FAIL / 3 NOTE with that config, the one FAIL ('blob not windowed/announced') being the exclusion taking effect, and 88 PASS / 0 FAIL / 4 NOTE with an empty XDG_CONFIG_HOME.",
  "limitations": [
    "0.50.0 blob-window defect: through the hook, `git show <rev>:<path> | tail -n K` returns lines from the ~8 KiB blob window plus a '[see remaining: rtk proxy git show ...]' hint instead of the end of the file (fixture: rows 1030-1033 plus the hint, where native git and 0.49.0 print rows 3996-4000). Neither acceptance script gates it; only the non-gating A2 differential caught it. This host mitigates it with ~/.config/rtk/config.toml `[hooks] exclude_commands = [\"^git show [^ ]*:\", \"diff\"]`, which also sends every `git show <rev>:<path>` and plain `diff` to the native command. adoption/bootstrap-linux.sh installs only the binary and does not render this file: a new host must create it (recipes/README.md), or the defect is live there.",
    "Pre-existing defects persist in 0.50.0 exactly as in 0.49.0: `find <nonexistent-relative-dir> -name x` exits 0 with no output (native: exit 1, 'No such file or directory'); plain `git log` is silently capped at 10 commits and `--no-merges` is injected, so `git log --oneline` drops merge commits; `python3 -m pytest` is rewritten to `rtk pytest`, which runs `pytest` from PATH or `python -m pytest`, not the named interpreter. `diff` on a missing file still exits 1 instead of 2 in the binary; only the host exclusion avoids it.",
    "Rollback hazard: 0.50.0 stores signed negative saved_tokens, and 0.49.0 reads them with an unchecked cast. With synthetic -500 rows, 0.49.0's `rtk gain --history` and `--all` (including `--all --format json|csv`) showed wrapped values such as 18446744073709551116, while plain `rtk gain` and `rtk gain --format json` showed none (out/negrow.out) and 0.50.0 clamps them to 0. The qualification corpus wrote 0 negative rows of 66 and production had 0 at qualification; the natural frequency is unmeasured. Before rolling back to 0.49.0, count `saved_tokens<0` rows read-only on a snapshot of history.db. tools/token-report's `rtk gain --format json` read showed no wrapped value, but the report also reads saved_tokens directly from history.db (tools/token-report/token_manifest.py).",
    "The landscape ledger does not move here: catalogs/landscape/foundation.json keeps the token-efficiency winner pin rtk 0.49.0 from the sealed 2026-09-22 layer-verdict packets. Host receipts recorded at 0.50.0 do not bind to that winner (scripts/host_receipts.py pin_matches) and stay unbound until a new verdict wave re-records the layer.",
    "Linux x86_64 only: adoption/pins-macos-arm64.json has no rtk pin and is unchanged; nothing here is macOS evidence.",
    "Local integration evidence with synthetic fixtures (fake pytest and ruff, generated git repositories, synthetic negative rows); the hook was driven directly with PreToolUse JSON. Upstream `cargo test` was not run on this host, and no fresh-session live Claude Code check after the switch is recorded.",
    "Provenance rests on checksums.txt and the GitHub API digest, both from the same release workflow; no signature is published, the attestation lookup returned HTTP 404, and the binary was not rebuilt from source.",
    "`rtk init` was not re-run. At 0.50.0, `rtk init --help` describes `--codex` as 'Target Codex CLI (uses PreToolUse hook + AGENTS.md + RTK.md)', so re-running the recipe's `rtk init --global --codex` would install a Codex hook that is not qualified; recipes/README.md now says so.",
    "One host (NativeStack, WSL2) and a prefix-flip switch; tools/rtk-0.49.0 and its archive are kept for rollback. The verifier's three minor defects (an unrelated ~/.claude/settings.json change outside the fingerprint window, the ungated `| tail` case, scratch written outside the unit dir) are retained in the artifact."
  ],
